From db44ff0f7c64360506fbb36737a034b9913d39ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:03:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compartments: the header of ICompartmentsPolicy names every
 method that needs MANAGE

The header said the first eight methods need MANAGE_COMPARTMENTS, but the
place methods (searchPlaces, getPlace, setPlace, getPlaceId,
getPersonaPlaceId) enforce it too. Only getProfile and getIdentity also
accept READ_COMPARTMENT_PROFILE (enforceManageOrReadProfile). Comment only.
---
 .../android/internal/compartments/ICompartmentsPolicy.aidl    | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/java/com/android/internal/compartments/ICompartmentsPolicy.aidl b/core/java/com/android/internal/compartments/ICompartmentsPolicy.aidl
index 77ec25d..812e2e5 100644
--- a/core/java/com/android/internal/compartments/ICompartmentsPolicy.aidl
+++ b/core/java/com/android/internal/compartments/ICompartmentsPolicy.aidl
@@ -9,8 +9,8 @@ import com.android.internal.compartments.CompartmentsPlace;
 
 /**
  * The Binder interface of the Compartments policy service (ADR-208). Every call acts on the owner
- * user's store. The first eight methods need org.oblivios.permission.MANAGE_COMPARTMENTS, which
- * only the exit app holds; getProfile and getIdentity also accept
+ * user's store. Every method needs org.oblivios.permission.MANAGE_COMPARTMENTS, which only the exit
+ * app holds, except getProfile and getIdentity, which also accept
  * org.oblivios.permission.READ_COMPARTMENT_PROFILE, which only the Settings app holds.
  *
  * <p>The transaction order is part of the contract with the app, which compiles its own copy of
-- 
